1
00:00:00,457 --> 00:00:02,827
(Bernadette:)Okay.
Thanks, Daddy.

2
00:00:02,826 --> 00:00:06,026
(Bernadette (on phone):)He said the only way to really
fix an old floor like that

3
00:00:06,029 --> 00:00:08,359
(Bernadette (on phone):)is to tear it up
and replace the whole thing.

4
00:00:08,365 --> 00:00:10,295
(Howard:)That sounds expensive.
Hang on.

5
00:00:10,300 --> 00:00:11,870
No offense to her father,

6
00:00:11,868 --> 00:00:14,098
(Raj:)but he's not an
MIT-trained engineer.

7
00:00:14,104 --> 00:00:16,034
(Raj:)Thinking and building
is what you do.

8
00:00:16,039 --> 00:00:18,209
(Howard:)MIT's motto is
"Mind and hand,"

9
00:00:18,208 --> 00:00:21,948
(Howard:)which just so happens was also
my motto as a lonely teenager.

10
00:00:23,313 --> 00:00:26,283
(Raj:)Oh, come on. We just need
to be more creative.

11
00:00:26,282 --> 00:00:29,922
(Raj:)What if you didn't step
on the floor at all?

12
00:00:29,919 --> 00:00:31,189
(Raj:)Like, what if you...

13
00:00:31,187 --> 00:00:34,557
(Raj:)swung on a rope
from the ceiling?

14
00:00:41,698 --> 00:00:43,668
(Leonard:)No.

15
00:00:43,666 --> 00:00:45,196
(Raj:)Okay. Um...

16
00:00:45,201 --> 00:00:47,601
(Raj:)Okay. What if you rig up
a pulley system

17
00:00:47,604 --> 00:01:02,024
(Raj:)and move yourself across
the room in a harness?

